From acfc40ed4ececc8f45aa43fea452949b67877518 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gus Bourg <gus@bourg.net>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 17:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 102/210] drm/meson: vclk: add deep color clock entries

Deep color runs the TMDS character rate at 1.25x (10-bit) or 1.5x
(12-bit) the pixel clock, which the fractional vid_pll dividers can
reach.

Add 10-bit and 12-bit clock entries for the 74.25 MHz (1080p24/25/30),
148.5 MHz (1080p50/60), 297 MHz (2160p24/25/30) and 594 MHz YUV420
(2160p50/60) modes. 2160p50/60 in RGB or YUV444 would need a 7.425 GHz
VCO, beyond the 6 GHz maximum of the PLL.

Signed-off-by: Gus Bourg <gus@bourg.net>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Co-developed-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
